Rules:
  [D1] Use Django MTV pattern (Model-Template-View).
  [D2] Use Django ORM for database access.
  [D3] Use class-based views for reusable patterns.
  [D4] Use Django forms for validation.
  [D5] Use Django templates for server-side rendering.
  [D6] Use Django admin for CRUD operations.
  [D7] Use Django migrations for schema changes.
  [D8] Use Django settings with environment variables.

Pros:
  - Rapid development
  - Batteries included
  - Excellent documentation

Cons:
  - Monolithic
  - ORM limitations
  - Performance overhead

Alternatives:
  - Flask (lightweight)
  - FastAPI (async)
  - Ruby on Rails

State: +

